    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39793" root="نسح" body-key="n">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَشَحَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسَحَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَشْحٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُشُوحٌ</span>, <i>He
drank a little,</i> (L,) <i>less than what would satisfy
him:</i> (S, L, K:) or, contr., <i>he drank until he
was full:</i> (L, K:) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتشح</span></b> . (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَشَحَ</span> <i>He gave</i> his camel <i>a little water to drink:</i>
(L:) <i>he watered</i> horses <i>so as to allay the vehemence of their thirst.</i> (T, L, K.)


